  "rhythm": "Songsterr's Raining Blood tab (lead guitar #1, revision 8446314), bars 23-28 read note by note: eighths with a quarter note closing each three-note chromatic group, 4/4, tempo marking 180 BPM from bar 23; Ultimate Guitar and guitaretab tabs agree on the frets. 24 beats = 8 s; eighths are 0.167 s, so it plays at full tempo. || 2026-09-29, redone and extended by acry (\"the heavy guitar/drums part that starts around 40 s\", bass + drums, same tempo): Songsterr s17904 (revision 8446314) tempo automation is 240 BPM for bars 1-3, 175 for bars 4-22, 180 from bar 23, all 4/4, so bar 23 (the old main-riff start, over tom fills only) begins at 29.1 s and bar 31 ('Gallop', where the full kit comes in) at 39.7 s. The entry now starts at bar 31: bars 31-36 (24 beats) replace the old bars 23-28, and bars 37-40 are the 16-beat extension. 180 BPM kept (the source tempo there). The gallop's sixteenth-sixteenth-eighth figure (a sixteenth is 0.083 s at 180, under the 0.08 s hold after release) is simplified to two straight eighths per beat, the two sixteenths merged into one eighth, so there is no slow-down; the eighth-note runs in bars 34 and 38 are exact. 40 beats = 13.3 s. Drums: style raining_blood_gallop, Dave Lombardo's part from the s17904 drum track bars 31-40 as one 40-beat pattern (sixteenth double-kick 36/35, open hat eighths, snare on 2 and 4, crash+china on the downbeat of bar 31, crash in bar 39 and china in bar 40 on beat 2), plus a 4-beat intro of his bar-29 tom figure (floor toms on 1, 1& and 2) with quiet hat counts on 3 and 4. Bass: Tom Araya's bass track bars 31-40 (eighth-note Eb pedal with octave jumps and the same run), shifted by the melody's +23 less two octaves (+11), D2..D#3. || 2026-09-30, extended and remastered by acry (\"extend ... and remaster ... match tempo/bpm\"): bars 41-44 of the same Songsterr revision appended (gallop, run, gallop, gallop; +23 as before, 16 beats, now 56 beats = 18.7 s). Tempo kept at 180 BPM: that is the tab's marking for this sect",
